     1	"""Canonical cloud status snapshot — local observation only, never SSH.
     2	
     3	This module produces the single "what is running?" truth document for the cloud
     4	worker, ``/workspace/.megaplan/status/cloud-status.json``. Every status consumer
     5	reads this same document: the Discord resident, watchdog notifications,
     6	``megaplan cloud status --all``, and humans debugging the box.
     7	
     8	Design rules (see ``docs/ops/elegant-cloud-status-resident-plan.md``):
     9	
    10	- Describe the cloud box from inside the cloud box. Never SSH.
    11	- Read only files the watchdog already writes: the canonical session markers in
    12	  ``/workspace/.megaplan/cloud-sessions/*.json``, the chain-health sidecars
    13	  ``*.chain-health.progress.json``, repair markers, ``needs-human`` markers, the
    14	  ``/workspace/watchdog-report.json`` verdicts, and the plan state files. The only
    15	  process namespace touch is best-effort tmux/ps liveness probing.
    16	- Be unit-testable with fixture directories and an injectable liveness probe.
    17	- Know nothing about Discord, resident conversations, or CLI rendering. Those
    18	  live in :mod:`arnold_pipelines.megaplan.cloud.status_format` and the resident.
