   615	    A chain (epic) is a sequence of milestones — the ``s1``/``s2`` plans. The
   616	    chain-health sidecar tells us how many milestones are done and the total;
   617	    from that we derive an overall epic percent and a per-sprint
   618	    done/in-progress/pending breakdown, so the resident can surface a
   619	    pre-calculated number instead of guessing. Returns ``None`` when there is no
   620	    milestone data to score against, so consumers skip cleanly.
   621	
   622	    The breakdown follows the chain's standard sequential progression: the first
   623	    ``completed_count`` milestones are done, the next is the in-flight sprint
   624	    (carrying ``current_plan``), and the rest are pending.
   625	
   626	    For the in-flight sprint we additionally estimate a per-plan percent
   627	    (``plan_percent``) from ``plan_state`` via :func:`_plan_stage_percent`, plus
   628	    the raw ``plan_state`` label. Both are omitted when there is no in-flight
   629	    plan or no recorded state, so the progress block stays clean.
   630	
   631	    The headline ``percent`` is the epic progress **with the in-flight plan's
   632	    stage fraction folded in** — ``(completed + plan_percent/100) / total`` — so
   633	    it advances as the current plan progresses rather than freezing between
   634	    milestones. Without an in-flight plan-stage signal it falls back to plain
